WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.385
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:15.484
Unit twenty-three: Philosophy of Education. Today you will debate aims using whether ... or ... clauses.

4
00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:18.436
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.621
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.612
Education.

7
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:29.706
Education means the process of learning knowledge, skills and values.

8
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:33.558
Education shapes both the individual and society.

9
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:37.104
Your turn. Say: Education.

10
00:00:39.967 --> 00:00:41.095
Education.

11
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:42.781
Knowledge.

12
00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:47.420
Knowledge means understanding gained through study or experience.

13
00:00:48.017 --> 00:00:50.446
Knowledge without judgment can be dangerous.

14
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.563
Your turn. Say: Knowledge.

15
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.262
Knowledge.

16
00:00:58.017 --> 00:00:59.053
Curriculum.

17
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:03.408
Curriculum means the set of subjects and content taught in a school.

18
00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:06.910
The curriculum reflects what a society values.

19
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:09.972
Your turn. Say: Curriculum.

20
00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:13.776
Curriculum.

21
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:15.680
Critical thinking.

22
00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:21.806
Critical thinking means the disciplined analysis and evaluation of arguments and evidence.

23
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:25.496
Critical thinking protects students from manipulation.

24
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:28.852
Your turn. Say: Critical thinking.

25
00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.887
Critical thinking.

26
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:34.698
Autonomy.

27
00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:39.227
Autonomy means the capacity to think and act for oneself.

28
00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:43.534
Education should develop autonomy, not obedience.

29
00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:46.524
Your turn. Say: Autonomy.

30
00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:50.472
Autonomy.

31
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:52.253
Purpose.

32
00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:57.212
Purpose means the reason for which something is done or exists.

33
00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.514
What is the purpose of schooling?

34
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:02.572
Your turn. Say: Purpose.

35
00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:06.307
Purpose.

36
00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.190
Pedagogy.

37
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:12.123
Pedagogy means the theory and practice of teaching.

38
00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:16.051
Progressive pedagogy values discussion over memorisation.

39
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.558
Your turn. Say: Pedagogy.

40
00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.355
Pedagogy.

41
00:02:24.117 --> 00:02:25.338
Citizenship.

42
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:31.415
Citizenship means the status and responsibilities of belonging to a political community.

43
00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:35.212
Education for citizenship teaches civic duties.

44
00:02:35.817 --> 00:02:38.933
Your turn. Say: Citizenship.

45
00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:42.917
Citizenship.

46
00:02:43.733 --> 00:02:47.326
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:48.183 --> 00:02:53.285
Visal, my parents want me to study whatever gets a good job. Is that what school is for?

48
00:02:54.383 --> 00:03:01.494
Whether education should prepare workers or citizens is debated. Each answer implies a different curriculum.

49
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:04.049
Can't it do both?

50
00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:11.877
Possibly. Whether the two aims conflict or complement each other depends on how one defines success.

51
00:03:12.983 --> 00:03:14.426
How would you define it?

52
00:03:15.517 --> 00:03:25.681
As autonomy. Whether a student becomes an employee or an entrepreneur, a mind that can reason is the lasting benefit.

53
00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:28.427
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:29.283 --> 00:03:31.956
Grammar focus: Whether or clauses.

55
00:03:32.256 --> 00:03:33.524
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:34.217 --> 00:03:37.807
Whether education should prepare workers or citizens is debated.

57
00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:43.143
Whether the aims conflict or complement each other depends on how success is defined.

58
00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:48.441
Whether students become employees or entrepreneurs, critical thinking will serve them.

59
00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:59.042
Whether… or… presents alternatives: Whether A or B is debated (noun clause) / Whether A or B, the result is the same (concessive: no matter which). Do not use 'and'.

60
00:03:59.783 --> 00:04:04.781
Be careful! Don't say: Whether education prepares workers and citizens is debated.

61
00:04:06.733 --> 00:04:11.055
Say: Whether education prepares workers or citizens is debated.

62
00:04:11.355 --> 00:04:12.623
Whether … or … (not 'and').

63
00:04:13.433 --> 00:04:16.225
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.360
What Is School For?.

65
00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.668
Philosophers of education have long disagreed about the purpose of schooling.

66
00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:31.773
Whether education should prepare workers for the economy or citizens for democracy is a question that shapes curricula, funding and teaching methods.

67
00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:39.782
John Dewey argued that the two aims need not conflict, for learning by doing develops both practical skill and democratic habits.

68
00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:48.397
Others stress autonomy: whether the content is science or literature, the aim should be to cultivate critical thinking rather than obedience.

69
00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:55.718
Pedagogy, accordingly, is not a neutral technique but an expression of a view of what human beings should become.

70
00:04:56.833 --> 00:05:00.974
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:01.817 --> 00:05:05.244
blank education should prepare workers or citizens is debated.

72
00:05:05.544 --> 00:05:08.989
A, Whether. B, Because. C, Although.

73
00:05:12.533 --> 00:05:14.649
The answer is A: Whether.

74
00:05:15.783 --> 00:05:18.224
The theory and practice of teaching is blank.

75
00:05:18.524 --> 00:05:22.828
A, pedagogy. B, curriculum. C, citizenship.

76
00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:28.645
The answer is A: pedagogy.

77
00:05:29.783 --> 00:05:32.549
The set of subjects taught in a school is the blank.

78
00:05:32.849 --> 00:05:36.514
A, curriculum. B, autonomy. C, purpose.

79
00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:42.206
The answer is A: curriculum.

80
00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:44.920
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:53.494
A, Whether he stays and leaves is unclear.. B, Whether he stays or leaves is unclear.. C, Whether he stays or leaves are unclear..

82
00:05:57.033 --> 00:06:00.554
The answer is B: Whether he stays or leaves is unclear..

83
00:06:01.717 --> 00:06:04.924
According to the reading, Dewey argued that the two aims…

84
00:06:05.224 --> 00:06:09.806
A, must conflict. B, need not conflict. C, are irrelevant.

85
00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:16.098
The answer is B: need not conflict.

86
00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:20.219
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:23.524
What should be the main purpose of education?

88
00:06:40.317 --> 00:06:41.829
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:42.129 --> 00:07:10.366
The main purpose of education should be to develop autonomous, thoughtful people. Whether they become engineers or farmers, they will face choices that no syllabus can anticipate, so the ability to reason matters most. Job skills are important, but they change quickly. Education should also prepare citizens who can judge evidence and participate fairly. These aims support rather than oppose each other.

90
00:07:10.666 --> 00:07:12.305
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:13.217 --> 00:07:17.239
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and whether or clauses.

92
00:07:17.539 --> 00:07:21.817
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

93
00:07:22.117 --> 00:07:25.233
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:07:25.533 --> 00:07:29.091
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

